9","definition":"The transition from downward flight to level flight just before landing.","example":"The captain executed the flare perfectly, and we lightly touched down.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["flareout"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cbeb95bad7f577eda1","definition":"A low fly ball that is hit in the region between the infielders and the outfielders.","example":"Jones hits a little flare to left that falls for a single.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["blooper","Texas leaguer"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be65ce95c2a02830f5","definition":"A route run by the running back, releasing toward the sideline and then slightly arcing upfield looking for a short pass.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ec34978ea4ffad43ca","definition":"Ellipsis of lens flare.","example":"The defect in question is the flare which frequently arises from the use of compound lenses when there is a very bright object in front, resulting in a ghost-like image of that object being thrown upon the plate. If the image of the object thus duplicated be in focus we designate it a \"ghost;\" if out of focus we call it \"flare.\"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:79070b46ef47cda21e","definition":"An inflammation such as of tendons (tendonitis) or joints (osteoarthritis).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["flare-up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dff31e79d1741990e9","definition":"A