er head, / I ſhalbe ſure to know her, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare","aflare","flarable","flareable","flare out","flarer","flare up","nonflared","reflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3025b657d335a1dd77","definition":"To suddenly happen or intensify.","example":"The genius of the poet [John Keats] flares up, dies out, and flares again, as if there were a dearth of fuel to feed it; and by this fault, more than any other, he is removed out of the class of great poets, and occupies but the second rank.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["flare up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["airflare","autoflare","earflare","flare angel","flareback","flare gun","flareless","flare nut","flare nut wrench","flare path","flarepath","flare stack","flare tower","flary","hyperflare","postflare","preflare","tripflare","trip flare","unflare","outflare","upflare","aflare","flarable","flareable","flare out","flarer","flare up","nonflared","reflare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:74466361e1da5c4a91","definition":"To suddenly erupt in anger.","example":"[H]e flared up very much when I told him I could not give him the schedule.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["flare up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figu